# Lex Fridman Podcast Semantic RAG Pipeline

An end-to-end Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) application built with [LangChain](https://www.langchain.com/) and [FAISS](https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss). This system turns unstructured podcast transcript archives into an expert consultation tool, allowing you to ask open-ended questions and receive structured, fully-attributed syntheses of perspectives from world-class experts.

## Architecture Overview

1. **Knowledge Retrieval (`FAISS`)**: Loads a local vector database containing pre-embedded podcast transcript chunks. When a query is submitted, it performs a semantic similarity search to retrieve the $k=10$ most relevant passages.
2. **Prompt Engineering (`PromptTemplate`)**: Injects the retrieved context and user question into a strict expert analyst framework defined in `prompt.md`.
3. **Response Generation (`ChatModel`)**: Combines retrieval and generation using LangChain Expression Language (LCEL) (`prompt | model`) to synthesize balanced expert viewpoints, areas of consensus/disagreement, and direct quotes with proper attribution.

